<description>&lt;p&gt;Bandits have escalated attacks in Niger, beheading village heads, killing residents, burning homes and a palace, and abducting civilians in villages such as Lumma Ba’are and Borgu. The Burkina Faso junta faces accusations from Human Rights Watch of targeting journalists, activists and opposition exiles abroad. These incidents occur alongside the ongoing jihadist threat that has produced 4,159 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP. The recent wave of beheadings and kidnappings marks a sharper rise in bandit violence compared with earlier reports.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiqwFBVV95cUxOMkdOUkUxZjJrdEJpaEk2bkZuQUxtSklMZDg5bVNJc2xJNjBKQng1NU96RjJCRkV4WkJzekJra2dHTDNxTVh3WTJsMThzOWtlUC0yY0hHb2dYX2xhbXVKZm02QUNGd1VRQzRVTHh5UUNXRk1XYjllN0RfNHpUbGtwMnF2cHZqcEVValZNc1NvbC1QTTBfY1RIb3VYT1JPMlpucGJMV1RvOGlTc00?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Guardian Nigeria News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiXkFVX3lxTE8yeGdBMXZQeHdkUUZ0UGlvRVM2LWtzTXpNaGVPT0JuYW1FWVZXUVZxall0S2hkcG1makZxUHp2aS1SNXNET0s2T3FTVXZFX2hoc1B2ZHVCMHlrRVc5THfSAWNBVV95cUxQbXZTdmkzWXpxci1iTDhkV3I1ZFVSNEtwM0pSbVMyRWxNUVlxM1RkSHRkRzZRWWtuNnU3RFVXenhmamtxNlZRX2VrYjVhX1F5SVNOWU5kVWg3bHFNeWF0TmxIQ0U?oc=5&quot;&gt;BBC&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimgFBVV95cUxQNWhMeG5TUTNic3FuOE1ZTENmT0cyZzZma1lRckdKenNFOGNobVBBOW5qM2MyR3NTRXJPeHFnSEpMdjBxbTdWaUpVWVNPek1fc0ZqdHJZZXQ1anVDSk94YWdpOGhhSm9IM0JTMTJJVTlXS3dsV2RUU0lBYk5Uak1DMldqTUZXRkJHVlF5TXFqaGY5QUR0THZnMGZ3?oc=5&quot;&gt;Arise News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxNeFZRWFNzazJGN3A3d2tNWUhLcE0yTktXVVQwMnRVeEJPd3NyakdMTjFnQkhGU0hpVExfa05iSTU5U09PXy12WVNwUDA5aTE5bE5MZTVRUzZrbGpkWlRkZ2F6azlyeS1PRE1PU2tiWDgxTlhLaEhMT2J3eUxRZ2U4S2F6RTM3MHhfMkg3Qm0zNktCTllnMy1WUkI5aWhxQ0hvRUZrb